course: dictionary
lesson: 9225
title: Somersault: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so look at the sentence around it. «In PE we learn forward somersaults on mats» means a roll of the body, head over heels. But «my stomach did somersaults» is not about a body turning over. A stomach cannot do a roll, so the sentence is about feelings: it means you felt very nervous.
explain: Look at the small words before somersault. «Toad turned a complete somersault» uses a and complete, so somersault is a thing that happened, a noun. «Somersault» can also be a doing word: «The car somersaulted in the crash» tells you what the car did, so it is a verb.
explain: Context also tells you when something turns over. The car did not just tip a little; it turned over completely, end over end. Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning.
fact: A somersault is a movement where you roll or flip your whole body head over heels, forwards or backwards.
fact: As a verb, to somersault means to do such a roll or flip, on the ground or in the air.
fact: A vehicle or object can somersault too: it turns over completely, end over end.
fact: Somersault can also mean a sudden complete change of opinion or plan.
fact: Flips and somersaults should only be learned with a trained coach, because they can cause neck injuries.
exercise: «In PE we learn forward somersaults safely on mats.» What is a somersault? | A loud shout of joy | A quick run before a jump | A soft mat used for gymnastics | *A roll or flip of your whole body, head over heels
exercise: Nadia reads «my stomach did somersaults before the test.» What does it mean? | She was very sleepy | She did a flip in the air | *She felt very nervous | Her tummy was full of food
exercise: Ben says the car «somersaulted» in the crash. What does that mean? | It stopped suddenly at the traffic lights | *It rolled over completely, end over end | It made a loud horn noise | It drove very fast in a straight line
test: After the news, Mia did a somersault with her plans and chose the beach instead. What does somersault mean here? | A roll on the grass | *A sudden complete change of plan | A loud cheer | A long walk home
test: «Flips and somersaults on a trampoline can cause neck injuries.» Why should you only learn them with a trained coach? | *Because they can cause neck injuries | To make the trampoline go higher | Because coaches are very tall | Because somersaults are always boring
exam: «Toad turned a complete somersault and lay amidst the ruins of the chairs.» What does a complete somersault mean? | *A full roll or flip, head over heels | A chair pushed against the wall | A wobbly walk across the room | A bowl of hot soup
